// stdlib/effects/naturality.sio
//
// `NaturalityG2` — the algebraic effect that the homology functor F: C_dial → C_𝕆
// uses to declare G₂-equivariance.
//
// Plan reference: project_octonion_homology_functor.md M2c (wk 6–8).
// Preprint: ocssm_preprint_skeleton.md §5.5 (functoriality of F).
//
// SEMANTICS (option A from the plan, "compile-time obligation"):
//
//   A function declared `with NaturalityG2` is a claim that, for every
//   element g of a discrete generator set of G₂ — the 14 standard Bryant
//   generators projected to integer Fano automorphisms (PSL(2,7), order
//   168) — the function commutes with g acting on its argument:
//
//     ∀ g ∈ generators(G₂_disc), f(g · x) = g · f(x)
//
//   The intent is for IR-emit to drop a `.lean` obligation stub at
//   `formal/lean4/obligations/<fnname>.lean`, closing via `native_decide`
//   over the finite generator × input table. Reuse the PSL(2,7)·168
//   infrastructure already proven in `SounioZeroDivisorBridge.lean`.
//
// CURRENT STATE (M2c — landed 2026-04-30):
//
//   - Effect bit 20 (= 1048576) is registered in
//     `self-hosted/compiler/lean_single.sio:18841` (`ety_parse_effect_name`).
//   - The compiler accepts `with NaturalityG2` and propagates the effect
//     through call-graph analysis like any other algebraic effect (Mut,
//     Div, …). Self-host fixed-point preserved (stage1 = stage2 = stage3,
//     md5 `af7e425c5b508ab96f6c7e7c320d82e6`).
//   - The Lean obligation generator is NOT yet wired. Declaring
//     NaturalityG2 today is a documented intent — the proof obligation is
//     deferred to M4. This is exactly the pivot state the plan §A.5 risk
//     register described as the kill-switch for Lean stalls (option B).
//
// WHEN TO DECLARE:
//
//   - Top-level `F: Trajectory → Knowledge<Octonion>` (the functor itself).
//   - `embed: i64 → Octonion` (witness that the embedding factors through
//     a G₂-uniform sample).
//   - Aggregations on Knowledge<Octonion> that are claimed to commute with
//     G₂ (e.g. fold-by-multiplication of an octonion path, since 𝕆
//     multiplication is itself G₂-equivariant).
//
// WHEN NOT TO DECLARE:
//
//   - Functions that depend on speaker labels in a non-G₂-symmetric way
//     (e.g. anything that breaks σ-pair symmetry; F2 conjugation is
//     non-trivial here).
//   - Functions that consume the rupture marker without re-broadcasting
//     it through the embedding (rupture is annotation-defined and
//     external to G₂).
//
// The effect is contagious: any caller of a NaturalityG2 function inherits
// the requirement (standard algebraic-effect propagation rule). To break
// the chain, write a wrapper that "absorbs" the requirement by closing the
// Lean obligation explicitly — see `formal/lean4/SounioNaturalityG2.lean`
// (M4).
